              "id": "d4365a55-3d4e-4034-87d1-e9716ba9ee6e",
              "name": "brand_voice",
              "value": "BRAND: Northwind Automations, a (fictional) workflow automation platform for B2B teams.  PERSONALITY: Practical, confident, a little dry-witted. A senior colleague who has done this before, not a salesperson.  DO - Lead with the reader's problem, not our product - One idea per email - Short sentences. Concrete details taken from the brief - Sound like a person  DON'T - Hype, superlatives or fake urgency (\"last chance\", \"don't miss out\") - Jargon the reader's role wouldn't use - Emoji, exclamation marks, ALL CAPS - Any promise, number or feature that is not in the brief  EXAMPLE OF OUR VOICE \"Most teams don't have an automation problem. They have a 'three people copy the same data into three tools' problem. Here's how to fix that in an afternoon.\"",
